{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The ambiguous pairs, ordered by the position of their first system and then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their second."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Such a pair runs in the order it’s written in, which is easy to change by accident. In the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"following schedule, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that ","type":"text"},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads, but nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"says which runs first:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement()","}","for ambiguity in frame.ambiguities() {","    print(frame.names[ambiguity.first], frame.names[ambiguity.second])","    \/\/ Prints \"Gravity Movement\"","}","","let ordered = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","print(ordered.ambiguities().isEmpty)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Order each pair with ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or mark it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" when either order is right. Systems without an access","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"always run alone, in the order written, and are left out. Call this method in a test to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep a schedule free of ambiguities.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"·(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"s"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"c","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":")) for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" systems and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"c","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ordered pairs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L525"},"extendedModule":"Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV11ambiguitiesSayAA9AmbiguityVGyF","title":"ambiguities()","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Inspecting a Schedule","generated":true,"anchor":"Inspecting-a-Schedule","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/d